{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/29832","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:35.775144+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Thanks for the repro, this is super helpful! I think you're right about the cotangent missing vma.\n\nWe have a potential fix, pending an internal review.","created_at":"2025-06-28T18:06:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/29832#issuecomment-3015964044","id":3015964044,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/29832","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc6zw_WM","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3015964044/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-06-28T18:06:49Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/3015964044","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12161222?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rdyro","id":12161222,"login":"rdyro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTYxMjIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdyro","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14262417?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yashk2810","id":14262417,"login":"yashk2810","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjYyNDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14262417?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yashk2810","id":14262417,"login":"yashk2810","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjYyNDE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yashk2810","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"### Description\n\nStumbled upon this while working on an implementation of NTK calculation.\n\nEssentially, when we have a function `f: f32[B@S] -> [B@S]` , calculations of the `jacrev` fail under shard map.\nI suspect this is because under a shard map the axis is vma and when passing the cotangent to `jax.vjp` should be declared as `jax.lax.pvary`.\n\n\n```python\nfrom functools import partial\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax.sharding import PartitionSpec as P, AxisType, reshard\nfrom jax.sharding import reshard\nfrom jax.experimental.shard_map import shard_map\n\n# Set up devices and mesh\nif jax.sharding.get_abstract_mesh().empty:\n    jax.config.update(\"jax_num_cpu_devices\", 4)\n    mesh = jax.make_mesh((4,), ('S'), axis_types=(AxisType.Explicit,))\n    jax.sharding.set_mesh(mesh)\n\n# Dimensions\nB, N, H = 20, 6, 8\n\n# Sample inputs\nW = jnp.arange(N * H).reshape(N, H).astype(jnp.float32)\nx = jnp.arange(B * N).reshape(B, N).astype(jnp.float32)\nxs = reshard(x, P('S'))\n\ndef f(W, x):\n    return jnp.sum(x @ W, axis=-1)\n\n@partial(shard_map,\n         in_specs=(P(None,None), P('S', None)),  # W is replicated, x is sharded on batch dim\n         out_specs=P('S', None),         # output is sharded on batch dim\n         mesh=mesh)\ndef f_jac_sharded(W, x_shard):\n    print('fj', jax.typeof(W), jax.typeof(x_shard))\n    return jax.jacrev(f, argnums=1)(W, x_shard)\n\n\n#jac_nonsharded = jax.jacrev(f, argnums=1)(W, x)\n#jac_sharded = jax.jacrev(f, argnums=1)(W, xs)\njac_via_shardmap = f_jac_sharded(W, xs)\n\n```\n\nerror:\n```python\nValueError                                Traceback (most recent call last)\nCell In[3], line 38\n     33     return jax.jacrev(f, argnums=1)(W, x_shard)\n     36 #jac_nonsharded = jax.jacrev(f, argnums=1)(W, x)\n     37 #jac_sharded = jax.jacrev(f, argnums=1)(W, xs)\n---> 38 jac_via_shardmap = f_jac_sharded(W, xs)\n\n    [... skipping hidden 12 frame]\n\nCell In[3], line 33, in f_jac_sharded(W, x_shard)\n     27 @partial(shard_map,\n     28          in_specs=(P(None,None), P('S', None)),  # W is replicated, x is sharded on batch dim\n     29          out_specs=P('S', None),         # output is sharded on batch dim\n     30          mesh=mesh)\n     31 def f_jac_sharded(W, x_shard):\n     32     print('fj', jax.typeof(W), jax.typeof(x_shard))\n---> 33     return jax.jacrev(f, argnums=1)(W, x_shard)\n\n    [... skipping hidden 10 frame]\n\nFile ~/Documents/pythonenvs/netket_pro/lib/python3.13/site-packages/jax/_src/api.py:2043, in _vjp_pullback_wrapper(name, out_primal_avals, io_tree, fun, *py_args_)\n   2040   ct_aval_expected = aval.to_tangent_aval()\n   2041   if (not core.typecompat(ct_aval, ct_aval_expected) and\n   2042       not _temporary_dtype_exception(ct_aval, ct_aval_expected)):\n-> 2043     raise ValueError(\n   2044         \"unexpected JAX type (e.g. shape/dtype) for argument to vjp function: \"\n   2045         f\"got {ct_aval.str_short()}, but expected {ct_aval_expected.str_short()} \"\n   2046         f\"because the corresponding output of the function {name} had JAX type \"\n   2047         f\"{aval.str_short()}\")\n   2048 ans = fun(*args)\n   2049 return tree_unflatten(out_tree, ans)\n\nValueError: unexpected JAX type (e.g. shape/dtype) for argument to vjp function: got float32[5], but expected float32[5]{V:S} because the corresponding output of the function f had JAX type float32[5]{V:S}\n``\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\n```python\n   ...:\njax:    0.7.0.dev20250628+1bd905a46\njaxlib: 0.6.2\nnumpy:  2.2.6\npython: 3.13.3 (main, Apr  9 2025, 03:47:57) [Clang 20.1.0 ]\ndevice info: cpu-4, 4 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Darwin', node='mbp-10841385', release='24.5.0', version='Darwin Kernel Version 24.5.0: Tue Apr 22 19:54:49 PDT 2025; root:xnu-11417.121.6~2/RELEASE_ARM64_T6000', machine='arm64')\nJAX_NUM_CPU_DEVICES=4\n```","closed_at":"2025-06-28T19:05:38Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/44061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.